Leo: I felt exactly the same last year. The trick that helped me most was simply practising out loud, again and again, until the words felt natural.
Mia: I''ve read my speech silently about ten times, but I still freeze when I try to say it aloud.
Leo: Reading silently isn''t enough. Stand up, use your hands, and say it to the mirror. Record yourself too, so you can hear your speed.
Mia: That''s a good idea. I always rush when I''m nervous, so people can''t follow me.
Leo: Then breathe slowly before you begin, and find one friendly face in the crowd to speak to. It makes the whole room feel smaller.
Mia: Speak to one person at a time. I''ll try that. Thanks, Leo — I feel a little braver already.', '米娅周五要参加演讲比赛,十分紧张,一想到上台手就发抖。里奥说去年自己也一样,最有用的办法是反复大声练习,直到说得自然。米娅说她默读了十遍,但出声就卡壳。里奥建议她站起来、用手势、对着镜子说,还要录音听语速。米娅承认自己一紧张就语速过快,别人跟不上。里奥让她开口前慢慢呼吸,并在观众中找一张友善的脸来交流,这样整个房间会显得小一些。米娅决定试试,觉得勇敢了一些。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is Mia worried about?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A speech contest later in the week","A maths exam on Friday","A school sports day","A music performance"]},{"q":"What does Leo say helped him most last year?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Reading the speech silently","Practising aloud many times","Memorising other people''s speeches","Avoiding the stage completely"]},{"q":"Why does Leo suggest recording yourself?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To check your speaking speed","To share the talk online","To shorten the speech","To copy a friend''s voice"]},{"q":"What problem does Mia admit she has when nervous?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She speaks too quietly","She talks too fast for people to follow","She forgets to smile","She stares at the floor"]},{"q":"What does Leo recommend doing during the speech?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Closing your eyes the whole time","Reading straight from the page","Looking at one friendly face in the crowd","Walking off the stage to relax"]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U1', 'sufe');
Ben: I like that. Reading the labels must be really hard for them, especially when no one is nearby to ask.
Sara: Exactly. So what if we design an app that connects a shopper to a call centre full of volunteers?
Ben: The shopper points the phone camera at a product, and a volunteer reads the label aloud through the speaker.
Sara: That''s the heart of it. The clever part is that it uses people, not just a machine, so it can handle anything unusual.
Ben: We should make the button very large and easy to find by touch, so the user never has to see the screen.
Sara: Good thinking. Let''s write up the idea and submit it to the students'' union before Friday.', '为科技周项目,萨拉提议解决一个真实的交流难题:帮盲人购物。本同意,认为读商品标签对他们很难,尤其身边无人可问时。萨拉设想做一个把购物者连到志愿者呼叫中心的App:购物者用手机摄像头对准商品,志愿者通过扬声器读出标签。萨拉说妙处在于靠人而非单纯机器,能应对各种特殊情况。本建议把按钮做得很大、便于触摸,用户无需看屏幕。萨拉赞同,决定周五前写好方案交给学生会。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What problem does the group decide to solve?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Helping blind people do their shopping","Cleaning the school library","Saving money on phone bills","Teaching maths online"]},{"q":"How would the app help a shopper read a label?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It prints the label on paper","A volunteer reads it aloud after seeing it through the camera","It sends a text message to a friend","It plays loud music"]},{"q":"Why does Sara think using volunteers is clever?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Volunteers work for free forever","Machines are always broken","People can handle unusual situations a machine might miss","It makes the app cheaper to sell"]},{"q":"What design feature does Ben suggest?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A bright flashing screen","A loud alarm bell","A tiny secret switch","A very large button easy to find by touch"]},{"q":"What will they do before Friday?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Submit the idea to the students'' union","Sell the app to a company","Open a real shop","Cancel the project"]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U1', 'sufe');
Anna: Yes, please. I know I made some mistakes. The beginning felt the hardest.
Mr Reed: Actually your opening question was excellent — it made us all curious. But you read too much from your notes in the middle.
Anna: I was afraid of forgetting my points, so I kept looking down at the page.
Mr Reed: That''s natural. Next time, write only key words on a small card, then look up and talk to us. Your eyes are part of the message.
Anna: And I stood very still the whole time. Should I move more?
Mr Reed: A little. Step forward when you make an important point. It adds energy. Overall, a strong start — keep practising.', '里德老师称赞安娜勇敢地完成了第一次演讲,并提出改进建议。安娜请老师指点,说开头最难。里德说她开场的提问很棒、引起了大家好奇,但中间太多照着笔记念。安娜解释怕忘记要点,所以一直低头看稿。里德说这很正常,建议下次只在小卡片上写关键词,然后抬头与听众交流,因为眼神也是信息的一部分。安娜问自己全程站着不动,是否该多走动。里德说可以稍微走动,在讲到要点时向前一步,能增添活力。总体开局不错,要继续练习。', 'uk_male', '[{"q":"What does Mr Reed praise about Anna''s speech?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Her very long ending","Her loud and fast voice","Her opening question made the audience curious","Her colourful slides"]},{"q":"What was the main weakness in the middle of her talk?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["She spoke too quietly to hear","She told too many jokes","She finished far too early","She read too much from her notes"]},{"q":"Why did Anna keep looking down at the page?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["She was afraid of forgetting her points","She had dropped her pen","She was reading a different book","She felt sleepy"]},{"q":"What does Mr Reed suggest she use next time?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A full written script","A small card with only key words","A loudspeaker","A large picture book"]},{"q":"What does Mr Reed say about moving on stage?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Never move at all","Run from side to side constantly","Step forward a little when making an important point","Sit down for the whole talk"]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U1', 'sufe');

